# Dependencies

Source: `governance/policies/dependencies.md` · Checklist: `checklists/dependency.md`

- A new dependency is at least MEDIUM risk; auth/crypto/build-pipeline dependencies are HIGH.
- Prefer: no dependency > standard library > existing dependency > new dependency.
- AI-generated package names are never used unverified (hallucinated and typosquatted packages exist).
- Before proposing, verify and cite: existence in the official registry, exact name, maintainer, recency,
  vulnerabilities, licence, transitive dependencies, alternatives, actual necessity.
  Unchecked items are marked `REQUIRES VALIDATION`.
- Installing is a protected action: propose first, install only after explicit approval.
- Major version upgrades are treated like new dependencies. Unexpected lockfile churn is a finding.

```text
❌ "Add `react-easy-datepicker-pro`" (unverified name)
✅ "RECOMMENDATION: use existing `date-fns` (already in package.json). No new dependency needed."
```
